<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Party of the Democratic Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1989</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as PRD</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Party of the Democratic Revolution (PRD) is a left-wing Mexican political party founded in 1989 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuauhtemoc">Cuauhtémoc</a> Cárdenas and other dissidents from the ruling PRI, together with parties of the left, after the disputed election of 1988. It governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> from 1997 to 2018 and was the main left opposition until many members left for Morena. It lost its national registration after the 2024 elections.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/party-of-the-democratic-revolution.jpg" alt="Party of the Democratic Revolution" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PRD_logo_(Mexico).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
